{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nTask SE-PE-01: Grammar-guided node reduction on a parse tree.\n\nThe rules are:\n1. Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes (process deeper nodes first)\n2. Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children\n3. Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\n4. Use node ID as the stable tie-break at equal depth\n5. Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order\n\nLet me think through the algorithm:\n\n1. Build the tree structure\n2. Process nodes in order: deeper nodes first, ties broken by node ID (lexicographic? alphabetical?)\n3. For each node (candidate for removal):\n   - Skip if not removable\n   - Skip if it's the root\n   - Skip if its symbol is a required symbol\n   - Check if removing it would still leave all required symbols represented\n   - Check it has no retained children\n   - If all checks pass, remove it (add to removed list)\n4. Return retained_node_ids (sorted) and removed_node_ids (in removal order)\n\nWait, let me re-read: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\nSo a node can only be removed if:\n- It's removable\n- It's not the root\n- Its symbol is not a required symbol (wait, or is it that the symbol still has other representatives?)\n- It has no retained children\n- All required symbols remain represented after removal\n\nLet me re-read: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\nI think \"a required symbol\" means a node whose symbol is in `required_symbols`. But then \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\" - this suggests that even if a node's symbol is required, you might be able to remove it if other nodes with the same symbol remain.\n\nWait, re-reading: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" - this seems to say never remove a node whose symbol is in required_symbols. But the next rule says \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\"\n\nThese two rules seem contradictory. Let me think again...\n\nActually, I think \"Never remove the root, a required symbol\" means:\n- Never remove the root node\n- Never remove a node that IS a required symbol (its symbol is in required_symbols)\n\nBut then \"all required symbols remain represented\" would be automatically satisfied if we never remove nodes with required symbols.\n\nWait, but in the fixture, `required_symbols` includes \"root\" and \"s1\". Node n1 has symbol \"s1\" and is not removable. Node n4 has symbol \"s1\" and IS removable. So if we might try to remove n4...\n\nActually looking at fixture case 0:\n- required_symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n- Nodes with symbol \"s1\": n1 (not removable), n4 (removable, parent=n2)\n- n4 is removable, but its symbol is \"s1\" which is required\n\nIf the rule is \"never remove a node whose symbol is required\", then n4 cannot be removed.\n\nBut if the rule is \"tentatively remove only if all required symbols remain represented after removal\", then n4 could potentially be removed because n1 still has symbol \"s1\".\n\nI think the second interpretation makes more sense for the Perses-style reduction described. The phrase \"never remove a required symbol\" might mean \"never remove ALL instances of a required symbol\" - i.e., you can remove an individual node with a required symbol as long as at least one other node with that symbol remains retained.\n\nLet me go with this interpretation:\n- A node can be tentatively removed if:\n  1. `removable` is True\n  2. It's not the root\n  3. After removing it, all required symbols still have at least one retained node representing them\n  4. It has no retained children (at the time of considering it)\n\nProcessing order: deeper nodes first, ties broken by node ID (lexicographic sort).\n\nLet me trace through case 0:\nNodes:\n- root: depth=0, removable=False, symbol=\"root\"\n- n1: depth=1, removable=False, symbol=\"s1\"\n- n2: depth=1, removable=True, symbol=\"s2\"\n- n3: depth=1, removable=False, symbol=\"s0\"\n- n4: depth=2, removable=True, symbol=\"s1\", parent=n2\n- n5: depth=2, removable=False, symbol=\"s2\", parent=n3\n- n6: depth=2, removable=True, symbol=\"s0\", parent=n1\n\nProcessing order (deeper first, then by ID):\ndepth=2: n4, n5, n6 (sorted by ID)\ndepth=1: n1, n2, n3 (sorted by ID)\ndepth=0: root\n\nProcess n4 (depth=2, removable=True, symbol=\"s1\"):\n- Has no retained children (it's a leaf initially)\n- Is s1 still represented if we remove n4? n1 has symbol s1, so yes\n- Is root still represented? yes\n- Remove n4! → removed = [n4]\n\nProcess n5 (depth=2, removable=False):\n- Not removable, skip\n\nProcess n6 (depth=2, removable=True, symbol=\"s0\"):\n- Has no retained children\n- Is root still represented? yes\n- Is s1 still represented? yes (n1 still retained)\n- Remove n6! → removed = [n4, n6]\n\nProcess n1 (depth=1, removable=False):\n- Not removable, skip\n\nProcess n2 (depth=1, removable=True, symbol=\"s2\"):\n- Check retained children: n4 was removed. Any other children of n2? No. So n2 has no retained children.\n- Is root still represented? yes\n- Is s1 still represented? yes (n1)\n- Remove n2! → removed = [n4, n6, n2]\n\nProcess n3 (depth=1, removable=False):\n- Not removable, skip\n\nProcess root (depth=0, removable=False):\n- Not removable, skip\n\nRetained: root, n1, n3, n5\nRemoved: n4, n6, n2\n\nThat seems reasonable. Let me code this up.\n\nFor the tie-breaking: \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth\" - so sort by (depth descending, node_id ascending for tie-breaking).\n\nNode IDs like \"root\", \"n1\", \"n2\" etc. - lexicographic sort: n1 \u003c n2 \u003c n3 \u003c n4 \u003c n5 \u003c n6 \u003c root.\n\nLet me code the solution:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Build node lookup\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    \n    # Build children map\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    for n in nodes:\n        for field in [\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"]:\n            if field not in n:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Missing field {field} in node\")\n    \n    # Track retained set\n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    removed_order = []\n    \n    # Sort nodes: deeper first, then by node ID for ties\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Skip if not removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip root (also covered by removable=False but be explicit)\n        if node[\"parent\"] is None:\n            continue\n        \n        # Check: no retained children\n        has_retained_children = any(c in retained for c in children[nid])\n        if has_retained_children:\n            continue\n        \n        # Check: all required symbols still represented after removal\n        # Count symbols among retained nodes (excluding this one)\n        symbol_counts = {}\n        for rid in retained:\n            if rid == nid:\n                continue\n            sym = node_map[rid][\"symbol\"]\n            symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) + 1\n        \n        all_required_present = all(symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) \u003e 0 for sym in required_symbols)\n        \n        if all_required_present:\n            retained.remove(nid)\n            removed_order.append(nid)\n    \n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted\n    }\n```\n\nWait, \"Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order\" - so retained_node_ids should be sorted, and removed_node_ids should be in the order they were removed (not sorted).\n\nThe symbol_counts computation inside the loop is O(n) per node which is a bit inefficient but fine for small cases. Let me optimize slightly:\n\nActually let me use a more efficient approach - maintain a set of symbols currently retained:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Build node lookup\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    \n    # Build children map\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    for n in nodes:\n        for field in [\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"]:\n            if field not in n:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Missing required field '{field}' in node {n.get('id', '?')}\")\n    \n    # Track retained set and symbol counts\n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    symbol_count = {}\n    for n in nodes:\n        sym = n[\"symbol\"]\n        symbol_count[sym] = symbol_count.get(sym, 0) + 1\n    \n    removed_order = []\n    \n    # Sort nodes: deeper first, then by node ID (lexicographic) for ties\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Skip if not removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip root\n        if node[\"parent\"] is None:\n            continue\n        \n        # Check: no retained children\n        has_retained_children = any(c in retained for c in children[nid])\n        if has_retained_children:\n            continue\n        \n        # Check: all required symbols still represented after removal\n        sym = node[\"symbol\"]\n        # If this node's symbol is required and it's the last one, can't remove\n        if sym in required_symbols and symbol_count[sym] \u003c= 1:\n            continue\n        \n        # Check all other required symbols still have representation\n        # (they do since we're only removing this node's symbol)\n        all_required_ok = True\n        for req_sym in required_symbols:\n            if req_sym == sym:\n                if symbol_count[req_sym] \u003c= 1:\n                    all_required_ok = False\n                    break\n            else:\n                if symbol_count.get(req_sym, 0) \u003c= 0:\n                    all_required_ok = False\n                    break\n        \n        if all_required_ok:\n            retained.remove(nid)\n            symbol_count[sym] -= 1\n            removed_order.append(nid)\n    \n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted\n    }\n```\n\nHmm, but this symbol_count tracks counts among ALL nodes, not just retained ones. When we remove a node, we decrement symbol_count. This is equivalent to tracking only retained node symbol counts. That's correct.\n\nActually let me simplify - the initial symbol_count should start with all nodes (which are all retained initially), and as we remove nodes, we decrement. This is correct.\n\nLet me trace through case 0 again with this code:\n\nInitial retained: {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, n6}\nsymbol_count: {root: 1, s1: 2, s2: 2, s0: 2}\n\nsorted_nodes by (-depth, id):\ndepth=2: n4 (s1), n5 (s2), n6 (s0)\ndepth=1: n1 (s1), n2 (s2), n3 (s0)\ndepth=0: root\n\nProcess n4: removable=True, parent=n2\n- children of n4: [] (n4 has no children in this tree)\n- sym=s1, required, symbol_count[s1]=2 \u003e 1, OK\n- all required: root (count=1\u003e0 OK), s1 (count=2\u003e1 OK) → all_required_ok=True\n- Remove n4: retained={root,n1,n2,n3,n5,n6}, symbol_count[s1]=1, removed_order=[n4]\n\nProcess n5: removable=False → skip\n\nProcess n6: removable=True, parent=n1\n- children of n6: [] \n- sym=s0, not required\n- all required: root (1\u003e0 OK), s1 (1\u003e0 OK) → OK\n- Remove n6: retained={root,n1,n2,n3,n5}, symbol_count[s0]=1, removed_order=[n4,n6]\n\nProcess n1: removable=False → skip\n\nProcess n2: removable=True, parent=root\n- children of n2: [n4] - is n4 in retained? No (was removed)\n- sym=s2, not required\n- all required: root (1\u003e0 OK), s1 (1\u003e0 OK) → OK\n- Remove n2: retained={root,n1,n3,n5}, symbol_count[s2]=1, removed_order=[n4,n6,n2]\n\nProcess n3: removable=False → skip\n\nProcess root: removable=False → skip\n\nResult:\n- removed_node_ids: [\"n4\", \"n6\", \"n2\"]\n- retained_node_ids: sorted([\"root\", \"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\"]) = [\"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\n\nThis looks correct to me. The algorithm properly implements depth-first (deepest first), with ID tie-breaking, and checks required symbol preservation.\n\nNow let me write the final implementation cleanly and encode it as JSON.\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n\n    # Validate required fields\n    required_node_fields = {\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"}\n    for n in nodes:\n        missing = required_node_fields - set(n.keys())\n        if missing:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Node missing fields: {missing}\")\n\n    # Build lookups\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            if n[\"parent\"] not in node_map:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Unknown parent {n['parent']} for node {n['id']}\")\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n\n    # Validate required_symbols exist in nodes\n    all_symbols = {n[\"symbol\"] for n in nodes}\n    for sym in required_symbols:\n        if sym not in all_symbols:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Required symbol '{sym}' not present in any node\")\n\n    # Track retained nodes and symbol counts (only retained nodes count)\n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    symbol_count = {}\n    for n in nodes:\n        sym = n[\"symbol\"]\n        symbol_count[sym] = symbol_count.get(sym, 0) + 1\n\n    removed_order = []\n\n    # Sort: deeper nodes first; ties broken by node ID (lexicographic)\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n\n        # Must be removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n\n        # Root has no parent; never remove root\n        if node[\"parent\"] is None:\n            continue\n\n        # Skip if any children are still retained\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\n            continue\n\n        # Check all required symbols remain represented after removing this node\n        sym = node[\"symbol\"]\n        count_after = symbol_count.get(sym, 0) - 1\n        if sym in required_symbols and count_after \u003c 1:\n            continue\n\n        # Remove node\n        retained.discard(nid)\n        symbol_count[sym] = count_after\n        removed_order.append(nid)\n\n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n\n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted\n    }\n```\n\nThis is clean and correct. Now I need to format it as a JSON string with escaped newlines and proper JSON encoding.\n\nLet me format the response as required - a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    # Validate required node fields\\n    required_node_fields = {\\\"id\\\", \\\"parent\\\", \\\"symbol\\\", \\\"depth\\\", \\\"removable\\\", \\\"utility\\\"}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        missing = required_node_fields - set(n.keys())\\n        if missing:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Node missing required fields: {missing}\\\")\\n\\n    # Build lookups\\n    node_map = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None:\\n            if n[\\\"parent\\\"] not in node_map:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Unknown parent '{n['parent']}' for node '{n['id']}'\\\")\\n            children[n[\\\"parent\\\"]].append(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    # Validate all required symbols appear in at least one node\\n    all_symbols = {n[\\\"symbol\\\"] for n in nodes}\\n    for sym in required_symbols:\\n        if sym not in all_symbols:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Required symbol '{sym}' not present in any node\\\")\\n\\n    # Track retained set and per-symbol counts among retained nodes\\n    retained = set(n[\\\"id\\\"] for n in nodes)\\n    symbol_count = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        sym = n[\\\"symbol\\\"]\\n        symbol_count[sym] = symbol_count.get(sym, 0) + 1\\n\\n    removed_order = []\\n\\n    # Process order: deeper nodes first; ties broken lexicographically by node id\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n\\n        # Must be explicitly removable\\n        if not node[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove root (parent is None)\\n        if node[\\\"parent\\\"] is None:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Skip if any child is still retained\\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Check all required symbols remain represented after removing this node\\n        sym = node[\\\"symbol\\\"]\\n        count_after = symbol_count.get(sym, 0) - 1\\n        if sym in required_symbols and count_after \u003c 1:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Commit removal\\n        retained.discard(nid)\\n        symbol_count[sym] = count_after\\n        removed_order.append(nid)\\n\\n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removed_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": retained_sorted\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01RXRLHUKSBpxdcYVjv1Br04","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2579},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2579,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":11,"output_tokens":4924,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4216},"service_tier":"standard"}}